\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces The bridge between the two monetary references, after the premise audit. The second column reports whether non-work maximizes the non-consumption index for every household; the third reports the median mass of the opportunity kernel on the domain the reference integral uses. That mass is not one, which is the premise that failed and the reason the earlier signed gaps were scale artefacts. The remaining columns are the bridge after normalizing the kernel on exactly that domain.}}{27}{table.17}\protected@file@percent }
